@jhedberg @joerchan I see what you mean, that a new callback for any pairing method will be more clean. We would like to act upon this callback, accepting or rejecting the pairing, so essentially, this callback will replace the `bt_auth->pairing_confirm`, making them mutually exclusive (with a Kconfig).

This also means my suggested `bt_smp_get_pairing_peer_info` function becomes obsolete, as the pairing information can be passed in the callback to the app instead. It makes sense not to use the packet definition struct, as we can then expand this information independently over time as a need arise for it - and flagging it even.

Did I understand your intentions correctly? If so, it makes more sense to close this PR and create a new one, as they will have little in common :)
